<GuideLayout 
  title="The Essential Activewear Tech Pack: Why Accuracy Saves Thousands" 
  type="TECH PACKS"
  description="Prevent manufacturing errors before they happen. A guide to creating comprehensive technical files that ensure your designs are executed perfectly."
>
  <h2>The Blueprint for Success</h2>
  <p>If you're launching a custom activewear line, the Tech Pack is your most important document. It bridges the gap between your creative vision and our manufacturing team's execution.</p>
  
  <h3>What's Inside a Professional Tech Pack?</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Technical Sketches:</strong> Precise front, back, and side views showing seam lines, stitching types (e.g., flatlock), and logo placement.</li>
    <li><strong>Bill of Materials (BOM):</strong> A detailed list of every component—main fabric, mesh inserts, thread type, zippers, and care labels.</li>
    <li><strong>Size Specification (Grading):</strong> Measurements for every size in your range (XS-XL), including tolerance levels to ensure fit consistency.</li>
    <li><strong>Colorways:</strong> Specified using Pantone TCX or TPX codes to ensure perfect color matching across different batches.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Why Precision Matters</h3>
  <p>Without an accurate Tech Pack, the sampling process can take 4-5 rounds, costing you time and shipping fees. A precise document can reduce sampling to just 1 or 2 rounds, accelerating your time-to-market by weeks.</p>
  
  <h3>Fitclo Design Support</h3>
  <p>Don't have a tech pack? Our in-house design team can help. We can translate your concepts or physical samples into professional technical files that are optimized for mass production.</p>
</GuideLayout>
